---
import { path } from '../lib/path';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { majors, wider, gold, universeCount } from '../lib/markets';
---

<Layout title="Strategy & Philosophy — Iron Hand Capital">
  <section class="page-header container">
    <p class="eyebrow" data-reveal>Our Philosophy</p>
    <h1 data-reveal style="--stagger: 1">Protect first. Grow always.</h1>
  </section>

  <section class="prose container">
    <p>
      Iron Hand Capital was built on a simple premise: most capital is lost not
      to bad markets, but to bad discipline. Two exposures sit at the centre of
      the book &mdash; gold and digital assets &mdash; and they are run on
      deliberately opposite principles, because they fail in opposite ways.
    </p>
    <p>
      Gold is traded actively, by a desk that does nothing else. Digital assets
      are bought outright and held. Neither approach would survive being applied
      to the other market, which is precisely why each is matched to its own.
    </p>

    <h2 data-reveal>No leverage where it can end the position</h2>
    <p>
      In digital assets we hold spot and nothing else. A leveraged position can
      be closed out by volatility alone &mdash; being right about an asset is no
      protection against being removed from it on the way there. Owning the
      asset outright means a drawdown is something to sit through rather than
      something that ends the position. In a market this volatile, the ability
      to hold is not a comfort. It is the strategy.
    </p>

    <h2 data-reveal>No single hand on the book</h2>
    <p>
      Capital in the gold sleeve is divided across several independent traders
      rather than concentrated with one. Each runs their own mandate, and no
      single trader&rsquo;s judgment, style or drawdown decides the outcome.
      Manager risk is a real and separate risk from market risk, and it is the
      one most often left unmanaged &mdash; we treat it the same way we treat
      asset risk, by not letting any one of them carry the whole.
    </p>

    <h2 data-reveal>Conviction is for entering, not for staying</h2>
    <p>
      We do not marry positions. A project that misses its targets, breaks its
      commitments or stops earning its place is cut or sold down. Position
      sizing comes before conviction, and downside governs every decision before
      upside is considered &mdash; concentration is a risk to be managed, not a
      strategy to be pursued.
    </p>

    <h2 data-reveal>Assets held away from where they are traded</h2>
    <p>
      Digital assets are held with an independent third-party custodian in
      segregated storage, not on a trading venue, and moving them requires
      multiple independent signing keys. No single party &mdash; ourselves
      included &mdash; can move them alone. The most common way investors have
      lost digital assets has never been the market; it has been the failure of
      whoever was holding them.
    </p>

    <a href={path('/approach')} class="link-arrow">See how each of these is run</a>
  </section>

  <section class="assets container">
    <p class="section-label" data-reveal>What We Trade</p>

    <div class="assets-lead" data-reveal>
      <h2>A universe of {universeCount}, and no more.</h2>
      <p>
        Depth in a handful of liquid markets beats breadth across assets we
        could not exit at size. The list is short on purpose, and it is the
        same list in every market condition.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="asset-rows">
      <div class="asset-row" data-reveal>
        <div class="asset-head">
          <span class="asset-kind">Digital assets</span>
          <span class="asset-mode">Spot &middot; unleveraged &middot; months, not minutes</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="chips">
          {majors.map((m) => <li class="chip chip-major">{m.ticker}</li>)}
          {wider.map((t) => <li class="chip">{t}</li>)}
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div class="asset-row" data-reveal style="--stagger: 1">
        <div class="asset-head">
          <span class="asset-kind">Gold</span>
          <span class="asset-mode">Actively traded &middot; several independent desks</span>
        </div>
        <ul class="chips">
          <li class="chip chip-major">{gold.ticker}</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="assets-note">
      Position sizing, weightings and the reasoning behind each holding are set
      out in the investor strategy room.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- Gate to the investor strategy room. The detailed material is NOT shipped
       in this static bundle — see /investor-access for why that matters. -->
  <section class="gate container" data-reveal>
    <div class="gate-inner">
      <p class="gate-label">Investors</p>
      <h2>The full strategy, in detail.</h2>
      <p class="gate-copy">
        Position sizing, allocation between the sleeves, how capital rotates
        between offence and defence, and the reasoning behind each holding.
        Released to verified investors rather than published.
      </p>
      <div class="gate-actions">
        <a href={path('/investor-access')} class="btn">Enter the Strategy Room</a>
        <a href={path('/investor-access')} class="btn-ghost">Request Access</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-header {
    padding-block: 64px 40px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 4vw, 46px);
    color: var(--text);
    margin-top: 16px;
  }
  /* The container keeps its full width and centring so the copy lines up
     with the heading above it; the reading measure is applied to the
     children instead. Narrowing the container itself moved the whole column. */
  .prose { padding-block-end: clamp(36px, 5vh, 56px); }
  .prose > * { max-width: 680px; }

  /* ---- what we trade ---- */
  .assets { padding-block: clamp(34px, 5vh, 56px); }
  .assets-lead { max-width: 640px; margin-bottom: clamp(26px, 3.4vh, 38px); }
  .assets-lead h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 2.8vw, 34px);
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .assets-lead p {
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.2vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .asset-rows { border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .asset-row {
    padding: clamp(20px, 2.4vw, 26px) 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .asset-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 16px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .asset-kind {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-size: 19px;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .asset-mode {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--muted);
  }

  .chips {
    display: flex;
    gap: 8px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .chip {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 12px;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--muted);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 6px 10px;
  }
  .chip-major {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-color: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 45%, transparent);
  }

  .assets-note {
    margin-top: 20px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  /* ---- investor gate ---- */
  .gate { padding-block: clamp(20px, 3vh, 32px) clamp(56px, 8vh, 96px); }
  .gate-inner {
    padding: clamp(28px, 3.6vw, 46px);
    border: 1px solid var(--accent);
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--accent) 5%, transparent);
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .gate-label {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .gate-inner h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: clamp(24px, 3vw, 34px);
    color: var(--text);
    margin-bottom: 14px;
  }
  .gate-copy {
    font-size: clamp(15px, 1.2vw, 17px);
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--muted);
    max-width: 58ch;
    margin-bottom: 26px;
  }
  .gate-actions {
    display: flex;
    gap: 12px;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }

  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .gate-actions .btn,
    .gate-actions .btn-ghost { flex: 1 1 auto; }
  }
  .prose p {
    font-size: 17px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--muted);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-serif);
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 26px;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 40px 0 16px;
  }
</style>
